From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Venus Build Fix <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bcm2711_defconfig: select CONFIG_VENUS

The tree carries a shared, architecture-agnostic Kconfig.venus with a
"VENUS" symbol that selects a large set of Venus-required options
(cgroups/netfilter/scheduling, WiFi/Bluetooth/USB-serial/CAN drivers,
i2c HID_CP2112 + I2C_CHARDEV for USB-connected IO-Extender hardware,
and more) - but nothing actually sets CONFIG_VENUS=y for this machine.
The 32-bit raspberrypi4 defconfig (arch/arm/configs/bcm2711_defconfig)
has "CONFIG_VENUS=y" as its literal first line; the arm64 one used for
raspberrypi4-64 never got the same line added, so the entire Venus
select cascade in Kconfig.venus has been silently inactive on this
machine. Confirmed against the actual built .config: all of
CONFIG_HID_CP2112's individual dependencies (I2C, GPIOLIB, HIDRAW,
USB_HID) are already satisfied, but CONFIG_VENUS itself reads
"# CONFIG_VENUS is not set" - so this is not a dependency problem,
just a missing opt-in line.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Venus specific]

---
 arch/arm64/configs/bcm2711_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/configs/bcm2711_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/bcm2711_defconfig
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+CONFIG_VENUS=y
 CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-v8"
 # CONFIG_LOCALVERSION_AUTO is not set
 CONFIG_SYSVIPC=y
--
2.43.0
